{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>וַיַּעְפִּלוּ וגו׳.</b> They erred in the ruling of their own judgment, for since they had rebelled against HaShem by their saying that He is unable to deliver the exalted nations into their hand, therefore they thought to remedy this by trusting in HaShem and firmly establishing the faith that He would deliver them, and they ascended the mountain. But HaShem was not reconciled, for their blow was still fresh and a decree had already been issued. And see what I have written in parashat Devarim (Deuteronomy 1:43)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:39.841657229Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}